"pretty," but not "completely."

I've never seen programming docs for the EB64 or EB64+ boards.  I
don't think it'd be easy to make them go, but they do not currently
work with NetBSD.  As far as I know, Alpha Linux supports them, so it
shouldn't be too hard to use their code as documentation, if no real
documentation exists.

If you get one of these boards, I can safely (as long as i'm still
